e m+1\\).  \nEquality can occur only for the three special lines listed in (3); therefore at most three of the \\(k\\) sunny lines can contain \\(m+1\\) points of \\(S_k\\).  \nAll remaining sunny lines contain at most \\(m\\) points. Hence the total number of points covered is at most  \n\n\\[\n3(m+1)+(k-3)m = 3m+3+(2m+1-3)m = 3m+3+ (2m-2)m = m(2m+1)+3 = \\frac{k(k+1)}2- (m-1) < |S_k|,\n\\]\n\nagain a contradiction.  \n\nThus no configuration exists for any \\(k\\ge4\\).\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n#### Conclusion  \n\nThe only non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two conditions of the problem are  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{k\\in\\{0,1,3\\}} .\n\\]"
